WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
London, 1854.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.210
John Snow maps cholera deaths, and they
cluster around one water pump on Broad

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.330
Street.

4
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.070
Cholera is an acute diarrhoeal infection.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.610
Most infected people have no
symptoms, yet pass the bacteria on.

6
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.610
In October 2010, Haiti reported
its first cholera outbreak.

7
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:29.210
By February 2019, Haiti had reported
820,000 cases and 9,792 deaths.

8
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.630
How did it arrive?

9
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.970
In imported food?

10
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.210
On a hurricane?

11
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.850
And why did it spread so fast?

12
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.010
In this mission, you'll
read a cluster map by date,

13
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.210
the way researchers traced
Haiti's first cases.

14
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.870
Then you'll weigh the
impacts and the response,

15
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.810
and find out why cholera
came back in 2022.

16
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.750
Your mission: explain how
cholera reached Haiti,

17
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.200
and why it spread so fast.
